            "text": "{\"strengths\":[\"Your written explanation gives a complete and accurate causal chain: drought lowers harvests, supply decreases at each price, a shortage occurs at P1, and equilibrium moves to a higher price and lower quantity.\",\"The diagram clearly labels the wheat-market axes, unchanged demand (D), and the supply shift from S1 to S2.\",\"You use precise equilibrium terminology, including movement along demand as price rises.\"],\"improvements\":[\"Extend S2 until it crosses D, mark the new equilibrium, and project it to the axes as P2 and Q2. This would make the diagram independently show the final outcome.\"],\"mistakes\":[],\"examinerComment\":\"Estimated practice mark: 3/4. The explanation is fully developed and reaches the correct equilibrium outcome. The diagram correctly shows a leftward supply shift with unchanged demand, but it does not show or label the new demand–supply intersection, P2, and Q2.\",\"studyNext\":\"Practise completing shifted-equilibrium diagrams: after every curve shift, always draw the new intersection and label both the new equilibrium price and quantity.\",\"assessmentFormat\":\"paper_2_c_to_f_diagram_and_explanation\",\"paper\":\"paper_2\",\"questionPart\":\"unknown\",\"levelRelevance\":\"shared_sl_hl\",\"assessmentSkills\":[\"diagram_explanation\",\"economic_analysis\",\"application\"],\"commandTerm\":\"explain\",\"commandTermLabel\":\"Using a demand and supply diagram, explain\",\"syllabusUnit\":\"unit_2\",\"syllabusTopic\":\"2.3\",\"topicLabel\":\"Competitive market equilibrium\",\"classificationConfidence\":\"high\",\"markingConfidence\":\"high\",\"diagramExpected\":true,\"diagramSubmitted\":true,\"diagramAssessmentStatus\":\"submitted_and_assessed\",\"workingsExpected\":false,\"workingsSubmitted\":false,\"workingsAssessmentStatus\":\"not_relevant\",\"attachmentContent\":\"diagram\",\"assessableEarned\":3,\"markBreakdown\":[{\"label\":\"Knowledge and terminology\",\"awarded\":4,\"available\":4,\"reason\":\"Accurately uses supply, shortage, equilibrium, and movement along demand.\"},{\"label\":\"Economic analysis\",\"awarded\":4,\"available\":4,\"reason\":\"Correctly explains the full sequence from reduced harvests to higher equilibrium price and lower quantity traded.\"},{\"label\":\"Application to context\",\"awarded\":4,\"available\":4,\"reason\":\"Directly applies the drought and unchanged wheat demand stated in the scenario.\"},{\"label\":\"Diagram\",\"awarded\":3,\"available\":4,\"reason\":\"Relevant, clearly labelled wheat-market diagram shows D unchanged and S1 shifting left to S2, but the post-shift intersection and P2/Q2 are not shown.\"}],\"bandRationale\":null,\"limitations\":[],\"componentEvaluation\":{\"diagram\":1,\"explanation\":2,\"diagramReason\":\"The diagram correctly shows unchanged D, S1, and a leftward shift to S2 with appropriate wheat price and quantity axes. However, S2 does not visibly intersect D and no new equilibrium, P2, or Q2 is identified.\",\"explanationReason\":\"The written response accurately explains reduced supply at each price, the shortage at P1, the rise in price, movement along demand, and the lower equilibrium quantity.\",\"incompatibleMechanisms\":false,\"mismatchEvidence\":\"\",\"labelingDeficiency\":false,\"labelingEvidence\":\"\",\"rootErrors\":[]}}"
          }
